comments.message:
Thank you for your work on this.

I think I found a bug. When a variable has an alias reference, the resolvedValuesByMode values do not reference the correct mode.

For example, my `neutral/1` has also light/dark modes, but the `bg/base` resolved values both point to the light mode.

{
"id": "VariableID:2821:310",
"name": "bg/base",
"type": "COLOR",
"valuesByMode": {
"2821:5": { "type": "VARIABLE_ALIAS", "id": "VariableID:7976:3435" },
"2821:6": { "type": "VARIABLE_ALIAS", "id": "VariableID:7976:3435" }
},
"resolvedValuesByMode": {
"2821:5": {
"resolvedValue": { "r": 1, "g": 1, "b": 1, "a": 1 },
"alias": "VariableID:7976:3435",
"aliasName": "neutral/1"
},
"2821:6": {
"resolvedValue": { "r": 1, "g": 1, "b": 1, "a": 1 },
"alias": "VariableID:7976:3435",
"aliasName": "neutral/1"
}
},

